ns that their military  commonwealth and charitable associations  are now going to revert back to the  queen so in terms of prince harry that  means his affiliation with  the royal marines ref huntington and the  royal navy small ships and diving  also his links to the queen's  commonwealth trust  the rugby football union the rugby  football league  and also megan's association with the  royal national theatre which she had  been given  by the queen who was previously their  patron and  also what is quite striking is also  they're not going to be able to  associate themselves with the  association  of commonwealth universities and i think  there was some discussion about whether  or not they'd be able to  keep their their links to some of those  commonwealth organizations but clearly  that has also  um had to go now we've also had a  statement  from a representative from the duke and  duchess  of sussex their spokesperson has said  as evidenced by their work over the past  year the duke and duchess of sussex  remain committed to their duty and  service to the uk  and around the world and have offered  their continued to sport  to the organizations they've represented  regardless of official role  they also say we can all live a life of  service  service is universal so  i think this shows today that that  divide between the sussexes  and the royal family in terms of how  they saw any potential future role any  possibility that  harry would be able to keep those  long-standing military affiliations  whether or not megan would be able to  continue to represent the royal family  when it came to the likes of the  commonwealth  that has gone that is over and  i think some of that has to do with what  has obviously been some very tense  discussions that have gone on  behind the scenes we also know this week  that the duke and duchess  have announced that they are going to do  that tell-all  interview with oprah i think it is  interesting that the palace today have  decided to put this statement out i  suspect they didn't want it to look  like they were maybe reacting after that  interview went out it's due to go out on  the 7th of march  and so yeah today it has been confirmed  by the palace that the duke and duchess  of sussex  are no longer going to be returning as  working members of the royal family  and as you've described there's been a  review process going on  over the past year but given that  announcement  about that interview with oprah winfrey  this is perhaps even less surprising  isn't it because to sit and publicly  take part in that interview did that  make  it incompatible to still be working  members of the royal family and  representing  the royal family on the world stage  look i think members of the royal family  they simply don't do interviews  like an interview with oprah this kind  of tell-all style that we're expecting  where they are going to talk about  setting up their new life in america  where megan is going to talk about what  it was  like stepping into the royal family  where megan is expected to talk about  how she's been dealing  with the public pressure and moving on  as  she's pregnant again and i think  when you looked at the fact that they  had decided to do this interview you  couldn't help but think  that maybe this was a reaction to the  fact that  the discussions behind the scenes had  not been going  in the way that they had wanted them to  we know that  in the last couple of weeks uh prince  harry of course  won a court case against the mail on  sunday with the mail on sunday  suggesting that he hadn't been  keeping in touch with the royal marines  in the way that he should have done and  after that there was certainly a lot of  his friends briefing that he really  wanted to try and keep hold of those  military titles  also of course 12 months ago we know  that the palace was saying one thing  they were saying look we're really  disappointed but this is how we see  things working  then harry and megan would come out and  say well no we're not happy with these  new arrangements  and certainly prince harry made it clear  at a dinner a center barley dinner one  of his charity dinners  and that he was not happy with how  things had played out between him and  other members of his family  and especially i think that that came  down to his military titles he is such a  proud man when it comes to  having served his country himself as a  proud army officer 10  10 years of service with the armed  forces and he really wanted to show that  he could  despite moving away to america could  continue  to represent his military family so this  will come  as an enormous blow especially to prince  harry  and i think you can't help but read into  some of these statements that  there is this ongoing rift um of course  i know that prince harry he didn't do  very much to kind of try to play that  down when he did an interview in africa  where he was asked about a rift with his  brother  and he openly admitted that sometimes  families don't get along and confirmed  really that he wasn't getting on  um with prince william but the the tone  of the statement from the duke and  duchess  of sussex it they they don't sound happy  and  that final sentence we can all live a  life of service service  is universal it does you do get the  impression that they do feel that  they have been pushed to one side um and  not been able to  to work in the ways that they wanted to  but also the final sentence  again of the statement from buckingham  palace  the royal family they still see them as  very much part of the family in that  final sentence where it says we're all  saddened by their decision the duke and  duchess remain much-loved  members of the family and i think today  on both sides there is going to be some  sadness about about  the fact that it has come to this and  that harry and megan have said that  there's basically no coming back  and the queen has agreed that and said  that 